--- body ---
## Context

Observed 2026-09-30 on padme: the DVC remote of this repository
(`/data/projets/dvc/oeconomia-climate-finance`, `.dvc/config.local`) and the
working DVC cache under `/home/haduong` are two btrfs subvolumes (`@data`,
`@home_haduong`) of the same partition, `/dev/nvme1n1p2`. The DVC
configuration names no other remote. The archived snapshots of JETP
documents (`data/jetp/documents.dvc`) therefore exist on one physical drive;
some of those pages have since disappeared from the web, so a drive failure
would lose evidence the M3 release is built from.

Not established: whether padme has a machine-level backup outside DVC. Only
the DVC configuration was inspected; the author knows.

Author's statement (2026-09-30, spec review wave 1, W1-22):

- padme runs a nightly restic backup of `/home/haduong`, `/data` and `/etc`
  to a Hetzner Storage Box, keeping 7 daily, 4 weekly, 12 monthly and 5
  yearly snapshots. It was found failing on 2026-09-30 (last snapshot around
  13 September; the exclude-file symlink was broken after the padme
  repository moved) and repaired by the author the same day.
- Zotero is the off-site copy now [M2]: each snapshot is uploaded one way to
  the Zotero group with its sha256 in the item metadata; DVC stays the
  working store until the M4 move (ticket 1510).
- `docs/jetp-operation.md` section 9 states both copies and the M2 test
  restore of one snapshot from each.

## Exit criteria

- [x] The author states whether a machine-level backup of padme's `/data` exists, and where
- [x] (Not applicable: a machine-level backup exists, restic to a Hetzner Storage Box, see log 2026-09-30) If none: the document bytes have a copy on another physical device or site (the operation spec draft proposes doudou pulling a copy after each push; an institutional or cloud store is an alternative), and a restore of one snapshot from it is tested
- [x] `docs/jetp-operation.md` (backups section) states the arrangement
- [ ] [M2] Every snapshot is uploaded one way to the project's Zotero group with its SHA-256 in the item metadata when it is pushed to DVC, and the objects pushed before the rule are uploaded once; no job reads from Zotero (`docs/jetp-operation.md` § 9)
- [ ] [M2] One snapshot is restored from the Zotero group and one from the machine backup, each checked against its hash; the test reads the date of the latest backup snapshot and fails when it is stale (`docs/jetp-operation.md` § 9, "Test of recovery")
